WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.160
- We've teamed up with Go RVing

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:04.360
to travel from Dallas to Waco,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.620
which is such a beautiful drive.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.140
And there are so many nontraditional trips

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.980
that you can take with your RV.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:11.070
And this road trip

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:14.410
with Barrymore was
anything but conventional.

00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:16.371
Wait till you see this.
(Drew claps)

00:00:16.371 --> 00:00:18.230
(upbeat music)
(horn honks)

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.163
Hello, Texas!

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.170
Drew, Look here, we are
at Trinity Overlook Park,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:25.200
the Dallas Skyline behind us.

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.910
This is a dream come true for me.

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:29.140
I have always wanted to go RVing,

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.550
and I know that you are an expert.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.550
- I've been RVing since
I had a driver's license.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.520
There really is no better way to travel.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.770
- Well, I have some stipulations

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.530
if we're gonna go in an RV trip, okay.

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:42.840
Number one, we need eat
good road trip snacks.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:44.170
- Like beef jerky?

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.700
- Yes, that's exactly what I'm thinking.

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.380
- I can't road trip without beef jerky.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.160
- And number two, can I drive?

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:51.330
- Well, I'm used to driving,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.820
but I'll be in your
passenger's seat any day

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.870
of the week.
- Yeah!

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.570
My big rig awaits.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.360
Let's start with a little beef
jerky first, just for energy.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.400
Say RV on three.

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:03.310
One, two, three, RV!
(camera clicks)

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:06.285
- I have a mouth full of
jerky, I can't say it.

00:01:06.285 --> 00:01:09.940
(RV engine roars)
- Yeah!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.030
- [Drew] We're actually
driving at five miles an hour.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.540
Can you believe that?

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:14.946
- All right, let's do this.

00:01:14.946 --> 00:01:15.833
(horn honking)
Excuse me.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.680
I think we're getting on the freeway.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.190
This is going to be a moment.

00:01:20.190 --> 00:01:21.470
- You're graduating.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:24.184
- We went from side street
to freeway real quick.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.430
(truck horn honking)

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:26.790
What are road trip games?

00:01:26.790 --> 00:01:27.900
I should have Googled it.

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.251
You remember I spy?

00:01:29.251 --> 00:01:31.260
- All right, let's play I spy.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:32.093
- How does it work again?

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:33.860
I see something, you have
to figure out what it is.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:36.783
- Which is gonna be hard
while we're driving.

00:01:36.783 --> 00:01:41.230
(laughing together)
- It doesn't work.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.155
- Do you wanna count how
many times I get honked at?

00:01:43.155 --> 00:01:45.200
(Drew laughs)
(horn honks)

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.880
That was one.

00:01:46.880 --> 00:01:48.050
I love that nod

00:01:48.050 --> 00:01:50.210
that people do like this when
you drive by someone like.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.043
Do you ever do that?

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:52.890
And like a one hand up wave?

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.235
- It gives me a lot of this.

00:01:54.235 --> 00:01:55.068
(laughing together)

00:01:55.068 --> 00:01:57.710
- I love that you're all
sunshiney and hi everybody.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:58.553
I love you.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.220
- Put a steering wheel in front of me

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:04.113
and I turn into the exorcist.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:09.140
- Oh, can we try barbecue?

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.423
- Yes, of course.

00:02:12.384 --> 00:02:13.952
(horn honks)

00:02:13.952 --> 00:02:14.952
Hello.
- Hello, hi.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:19.220
We want some barbecue.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.400
- You're in the right spot.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.240
- [Ross] So what makes
your barbecue so delicious?

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.690
- Well, we're famous for the brisket

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:28.100
and we were voted one of the
top 50 in "Texas Monthly".

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.480
- How does Texas do barbecue?

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.120
- Oh, Texas style barbecue
is probably the best.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.960
- Why?
- It is smoked meat.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:35.870
- Can we try some barbecue?

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:39.573
- Oh my God, look at this!

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.200
- Oh!
(Drew screams)

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.623
No, a tisket and a tasket,
put some brisket in my basket.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:57.831
- Oh my God, it's incredible.

00:02:57.831 --> 00:02:59.940
Thank you so much.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.160
I feel like I could eat the whole thing.

00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:03.780
- We'll just wrap up
that whole brisket to go,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.230
thank you.
- [Drew] Exactly!

00:03:07.724 --> 00:03:10.522
(upbeat music)

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:13.189
(horns honking)

00:03:14.164 --> 00:03:16.250
- Where's your favorite
place you've ever gone RVing?

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.580
- Joshua Tree when there
was a meteor shower.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:21.640
- Wow, I used to go camping

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:23.207
with my parents all the time, growing up

00:03:23.207 --> 00:03:27.110
and I would love sleeping in the RV,

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:29.440
sitting out by the campfire,

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.160
my parents just getting drunk.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.070
- That's about the only thing I relate to

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:35.963
about any of this scenario.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:40.627
- What is the most romantic movie ever?

00:03:40.627 --> 00:03:42.277
- "Breakfast at Tiffany's".

00:03:43.330 --> 00:03:47.370
I'm trying to think of
my favorite kiss too.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:48.980
Kissing is so hot.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:49.830
- It totally is.

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:51.160
- Oh my God.

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.130
- My first kiss with Wellie

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.410
was like 45 minutes after we met.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.140
- Shut up, I love it.

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:57.060
Why waste time?

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.190
Get in there.
- Why waste time?

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.373
Are we still in Texas?

00:04:00.492 --> 00:04:02.550
(horn honks)

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:03.543
Hello Waco!

00:04:10.082 --> 00:04:10.963
Right.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:13.883
- We made it!

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:18.150
- Thank you for making
my RV dreams come true.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.000
- Oh my God, you're so welcome.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:22.031
- One last selfie, ready?

00:04:22.031 --> 00:04:26.092
(camera film clicks)
(audience cheer and clap)

00:04:26.092 --> 00:04:27.791
That was so much fun.

00:04:27.791 --> 00:04:29.450
- Oh, thank you Go RVing

00:04:30.347 --> 00:04:33.620
for helping us take not
only such a fun trip,

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:35.650
but helping me realize my dreams

00:04:35.650 --> 00:04:38.260
of talking about this on this show.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:39.860
- I know, and my dream come true.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:40.693
I was driving that.

00:04:40.693 --> 00:04:42.273
You all see me driving that RV?

00:04:42.273 --> 00:04:43.166
(audience cheer and clap)

00:04:43.166 --> 00:04:44.690
- You manned that RV.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.960
- That's right, I did
with my girl by my side

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.770
in the open road out there.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.580
And for all of you at home,
RVing is for everyone,

00:04:53.580 --> 00:04:55.280
even people who don't see them

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.610
maybe as the typical RVer,
people like me, you can trust me,

00:04:58.610 --> 00:04:59.640
you've gotta try it.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.473
- It's so true.

00:05:00.473 --> 00:05:03.041
(upbeat music)

